# Instance ownership. This file is what makes governance mechanical rather than
# conventional, and it is the split recommended in the review: Curators own
# structure at low frequency, Reviewers own the queue at high frequency.
#
# Replace the placeholders with real GitHub handles, then turn on branch
# protection for the default branch with "Require review from Code Owners".
# Without branch protection this file is documentation, not a control.

# Curators: tiering, structure, configuration. Low frequency, strategic.
/tiers.yaml          @CURATOR @CURATOR_DEPUTY
/config.yaml         @CURATOR @CURATOR_DEPUTY
/.github/            @CURATOR
/product/            @PRODUCT_OWNER @CURATOR

# Reviewers: the intel queue. High frequency, clerical, deliberately plural so
# review never depends on one person being available.
/signals/            @REVIEWERS
/vendors/            @REVIEWERS
/assessments/        @REVIEWERS
